  "generated_text": "To determine the number of shirt-and-tie outfits where no shirt and tie are of the same color, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outfits without any restrictions:**\n   - There are 8 colors.\n   - For each color, there is one shirt and one tie.\n   - Therefore, the total number of possible outfits is \\(8 \\times 8 = 64\\).\n\n2. **Identify the number of outfits where the shirt and tie are of the same color:**\n   - Since there are 8 colors, there are 8 outfits where the shirt and tie are of the same color (one for each color).\n\n3. **Calculate the number of valid outfits:**\n   - Subtract the number of restricted outfits from the total number of possible outfits.\n   - Total possible outfits: 64\n   - Restricted outfits: 8\n   - Valid outfits: \\(64 - 8 = 56\\)\n\nThus, the number of shirt-and-tie outfits where no shirt and tie are of the same color is \\(\\boxed{56}\\).",
